  "tagline": "Tiny type-safe local JSON database for Node, Electron and the browser using plain JavaScript.",
  "description": "lowdb is a minimal library that loads a JSON file (or localStorage) into memory as a plain JavaScript object, lets you mutate it with ordinary array and object methods, and writes it back atomically. With TypeScript it gives typed access to the data and has no query language to learn. It is popular for prototypes, CLIs, Electron apps, small demos and test fixtures, and underpins tools like json-server. The library is effectively feature-complete: v7.0.1 (December 2023) is the latest release, with only occasional maintenance commits since. It is not a database in the transactional sense and should not be used for concurrent multi-process writes.",
